6. Full Method Specification
6.1 Method Schema
The method schema defines the structure of a method deposit.

It has the following fields:

method_id. A string. Required.

method_name. A string. Required.

description. A string. Required.

subject. A string. Required.

topic. A string. Required.

applicability_conditions. An array of strings. Required.

failure_conditions. An array of strings. Required.

prerequisites. An array of prerequisite objects. Optional.

worked_examples. An array of example objects. Optional.

proficiency. An object. Required. It contains level and last_assessed.

student_id. A string. Required.

date_learned. A string in ISO8601 format. Required.

date_last_used. A string in ISO8601 format. Optional.

related_methods. An array of method relations. Optional.

provenance. An object. Required.

stag_annotation. An object. Optional.

work_reference. A string. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

Each prerequisite object has:

prerequisite_id. A string.

prerequisite_type. An enum. The values are concept, method, skill.

prerequisite_name. A string.

prerequisite_description. A string.

Each example object has:

example_id. A string.

problem_description. A string.

solution. A string.

date_worked. A string in ISO8601 format.

result. An enum. The values are correct, partial, incorrect.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each method relation has:

relation_id. A string.

related_method_id. A string.

relation_type. An enum. The values are prerequisite, alternative, special_case, generalisation, related, independent.

relation_note. A string. Optional.

The proficiency level has four values:

novice.

developing.

proficient.

advanced.

