7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Method
function createMethod(method, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the method against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the STAG annotation is present, validate it.

Step 4. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. Generate a method ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 6. Insert the method.

Step 7. Insert the prerequisite records, the worked-example records, and the relation records.

Step 8. Insert the STAG link and the work link if present.

Step 9. Insert the provenance.

Step 10. Insert the moderation record.

Step 11. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 12. Return the method_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Method
function readMethod(methodId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the method. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the prerequisites, the worked examples, the relations, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Method
function updateMethod(methodId, method, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing method. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new method.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the method_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Method
function deleteMethod(methodId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing method. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the method_id and the status deleted.

7.5 Query Methods
function queryMethods(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the query.

Step 3. Read the matching methods.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the methods, the count, and the pagination.

7.6 Aggregate Methods
function aggregateMethods(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the aggregation.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the results.

7.7 Full-Text Search
function fullTextSearch(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the search.

Step 3. Read the matching methods.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the methods and the count.

7.8 Export Method
function exportMethod(methodId, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the deposit.

Step 3. If json, output the deposit. If provo, export to PROV-O. If turtle, serialize to Turtle.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the format.

7.9 Bulk Import
function bulkImport(file, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Parse the file.

Step 3. For each method, call createMethod.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the results and the count.

7.10 Bulk Export
function bulkExport(query, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the matching methods.

Step 3. If json, output the list. If jsonl, output one line per method. If provo, export each one.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the count.

7.11 Moderate Method
function moderateMethod(methodId, moderationStatus, moderationNotes, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "moderator"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing method. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Update the moderation status. Insert a moderation record.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the method_id and the status.

7.12 Method Map
function methodMap(auth, options):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read all methods.

Step 3. Build the map with subjects as regions and prerequisites as edges.

Step 4. Return the map.

7.13 Proficiency Curve
function proficiencyCurve(methodId, studentId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the method and the student.

Step 3. Read the worked examples and their results over time.

Step 4. Build the curve with the proficiency over time.

Step 5. Return the curve.

7.14 Method Comparison View
function methodComparisonView(methodIds, problemDescription, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read each method.

Step 3. Build the comparison by overlaying the applicability conditions and the failure conditions.

Step 4. Return the comparison.

7.15 Find Related Methods
function findRelatedMethods(methodId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the method. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Find methods with the same subject, the same topic, or the same prerequisites.

Step 4. Return the related methods.

7.16 Audit Log
function auditLog(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the query.

Step 3. Return the results.

7.17 Backup
function backup(auth, options):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. If sql, dump as SQL. If json, dump as JSON.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the output and the format.

7.18 Restore
function restore(file, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Load the database from the file.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the status restored.

